  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>First step involves the reduction of nitrobenzene to aniline in presence of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sn</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math>. Second step is a diazotization reaction&nbsp; where aniline is converted to benzenediazonium chloride in presence of nitrous acid, and third step involves the reaction between benzene diazonium chloride and beta-naphthol to form 1-phenylazo-2-naphthol&nbsp;an orange red dye.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d77ba067-6eb6-4c2c-8b04-084ed40b8214-26-06-2022.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 268px;\" /></p>",
